# CodeDNA

Local AI-code attribution with in-source provenance.

Tracks every edit in VS Code and classifies it as:
- **Human** — You typed it
- **AI-Generated** — Copilot/Cursor/Claude wrote it
- **AI-Modified** — AI changed your code
- **Ambiguous** — Mixed or unclear origin

Shows a live H/AI ratio in the status bar with gutter colors (green = human, blue = AI). Persists provenance as in-source headers (`codedna:` blocks) so downstream AI agents inherit attribution without rediscovery.

**Zero cloud. Zero network calls. Fully local.**

## Install

```bash
# VS Code extension
code --install-extension codedna.vsix

# CLI (for CI, scripts, headless use)
pip install codedna
```

## Quick Start

```bash
# Scan a repo and print attribution report
codedna scan .

# Show live ratio for current file
codedna ratio path/to/file.py

# Toggle in-source provenance headers
codedna headers on
codedna headers off
```

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────┐     stdio IPC      ┌──────────────────────┐
│  VS Code Extension  │ ──────────────────▶ │   codedna-core       │
│  (TypeScript)       │                     │   (Python)           │
└─────────────────────┘                     └──────────────────────┘
       │                                           │
       ▼                                           ▼
  onDidChangeTextDocument                  Classifier + SQLite
  Status bar, gutter colors                In-source headers
```

